  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/e7ca505879c9b628978a2be3fe2df4f3c248c2acc32e33a22cedbdf8cd4bd4da.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the population of a town $(y)$ recorded $x$ years after $2000.$\nThe equation of the trend line is $y=0.1x+53.$ Assuming this trend continues, estimate the town's population in $2026.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the year $2026$ is $26$ years since the year $2000.$\n\nTo predict the population in $2026,$ we need to substitute $x=26$ into the equation of the trend line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0.1x+53 \\\\  & =0.1(26)+53 \\\\  & =2.6+53 \\\\  & =55.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, according to this model, the population will be approximately $55\\,600$ in $2026.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=26$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable.",
